+# XNNPACK's AVX512-BF16 GEMM configuration unconditionally references assembly
+# microkernels (`..._asm_amd64_avx512bf16_broadcast`) that are not assembled
+# under MSVC, so enabling the feature here fails to link. XNNPACK enabled it by
+# default for the whole x86 family in
+# https://github.com/google/XNNPACK/commit/0363fd2f2b, and its `x86` config
+# setting matches plain `windows_x86_64` (MSVC) whereas the previous `x86_64`
+# setting only matched the clang-cl, clang and mingw variants. Opt back out to
+# keep the behavior this build had before that change.
+build:windows --define=xnn_enable_avx512bf16=false
+
